From d28f7812508de044701459e076afc940a7880a7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:51:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Files of parameters: line of the errors, errno restored;
 tfel-check: shall_fail refuses a success

- the line given in the errors of the files of parameters of the material
  properties and of the behaviours was always the first one: the counter
  is now incremented at each line;
- material properties: errno is restored after the reading of the file of
  parameters, when it succeeds and after an invalid parameter name. A
  value setting errno when converted (a subnormal number) made the first
  evaluation of the generic interface fail with the status -3;
- tfel-check: a command with the shall_fail option set to true which
  succeeds is reported as a failure.

Tests: the invalid value of the file of parameters of the test of the
material properties is on the third line, and the error is checked to
give it; a new case of the comparator of the behaviours writes an invalid
number of tokens on the third line (option --invalid-parameters-message);
new test test-parameters-errno.cxx (generic interface, configuration
stlpar-parunseq-gcc).
---
